### D1 hostile parent config (downloadDir escapes its own tree)
$ sutradhar nav http://localhost:1/   (cwd=<R>/hp/child; config in <R>/hp)
(exit 1)
Error: Invalid project config <R>\hp\.sutradhar.json: downloadDir "../outside-hp" resolves to "<R>\outside-hp", outside this config's directory "<R>\hp". A project config found by searching upward may only allow downloads inside its own directory tree. To allow it anyway, set SUTRADHAR_ALLOWED_DOWNLOAD_ROOTS, or load this file explicitly with SUTRADHAR_CONFIG=<file>.
forbidden dir <R>/outside-hp exists: false

### D2 same file loaded EXPLICITLY (trusted like an env var): accepted
$ SUTRADHAR_CONFIG=<R>/hp/.sutradhar.json sutradhar doctor
(exit 0)
Platform:        win32 (x64)
Node version:    v25.0.0
Chrome found:    yes
Chrome path:     C:\Program Files\Google\Chrome\Application\chrome.exe
Active session:  none
Config:          <R>\hp\.sutradhar.json (SUTRADHAR_CONFIG)
Config sources:  allowedDomains=default, downloadRoots=config, uploadRoots=unrestricted, dialog=default, viewport=default

### E config only
$ sutradhar nav http://localhost:1/    (env: {})
(exit 1)
Fatal: Navigation to "http://localhost:1/" was blocked: allowedDomains is configured and "localhost" is not in the allowlist (config.example). This is a safety guardrail — add the domain to allowedDomains if this navigation is expected.

### E env + config
$ sutradhar nav http://localhost:1/    (env: {"SUTRADHAR_ALLOWED_DOMAINS":"env.example"})
(exit 1)
Fatal: Navigation to "http://localhost:1/" was blocked: allowedDomains is configured and "localhost" is not in the allowlist (env.example). This is a safety guardrail — add the domain to allowedDomains if this navigation is expected.

### E flag + env + config
$ sutradhar nav http://localhost:1/ --allowlist-domains flag.example   (env: {"SUTRADHAR_ALLOWED_DOMAINS":"env.example"})
(exit 1)
Fatal: Navigation to "http://localhost:1/" was blocked: allowedDomains is configured and "localhost" is not in the allowlist (flag.example). This is a safety guardrail — add the domain to allowedDomains if this navigation is expected.

### cleanup: close the session the E block opened
$ sutradhar close
(exit 0)
Session closed.

